## 7. Kafka topic setup

Provision the topics through infrastructure automation, not implicitly from the application.

Example for a three-broker environment:

```bash
kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server "$KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS" \
  --command-config admin.properties \
  --create \
  --topic csv.events \
  --partitions 6 \
  --replication-factor 3 \
  --config min.insync.replicas=2 \
  --config unclean.leader.election.enable=false

kafka-topics.sh \
  --bootstrap-server "$KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS" \
  --command-config admin.properties \
  --create \
  --topic csv.checkpoints.orders \
  --partitions 1 \
  --replication-factor 3 \
  --config cleanup.policy=compact \
  --config retention.ms=-1 \
  --config retention.bytes=-1 \
  --config min.insync.replicas=2 \
  --config unclean.leader.election.enable=false
```

The checkpoint topic must use **`compact`, not `compact,delete`**. Compaction retains the latest value for each key; adding deletion retention can remove the state needed to prevent reprocessing. Do not tombstone completed-file checkpoints while those file identities might reappear. ([kafka.apache.org](https://kafka.apache.org/40/generated/topic_config.html?utm_source=openai))

Also require:

- Broker-side automatic topic creation disabled.
- Transaction-state topic replication appropriate for production.
- `transaction.max.timeout.ms` at least `180000` for the example configuration.
- ACLs restricting checkpoint writes and the transactional ID to this application.
- Output-topic retention matched to your downstream recovery requirements.

Kafka validates producer transaction timeouts against the broker maximum, and its production transaction defaults assume replicated transaction state. ([kafka.apache.org](https://kafka.apache.org/26/configuration/producer-configs/?utm_source=openai))

### Downstream consumers

For a Spring Kafka consumer:

```yaml
spring:
  kafka:
    consumer:
      properties:
        isolation.level: read_committed
```

Without this, consumers can see records from aborted transactions. ([kafka.apache.org](https://kafka.apache.org/41/design/design/?utm_source=openai))

